# Backend Rules — Node.js + Express

## Module System
- CommonJS only (`require` / `module.exports`) — do NOT use ESM (`import`/`export`) in backend
- All third-party clients (OpenAI, MinIO) instantiated inside their service file, never in controllers or routes

## Architecture Layers — strict separation

```
routes/       → define URL + HTTP method, attach middleware, delegate to controller
controllers/  → parse req, call services, send res — NO business logic, NO SQL
services/     → business logic, external API calls (AI, storage)
db/           → ALL SQL here as prepared statements — nothing else touches the DB
middleware/   → reusable Express middleware (upload, rate limit)
```

### Rules per layer
- Routes: 1 line per route (`router.post('/', upload.single('image'), handler)`)
- Controllers: max 30 lines, no direct DB access, no `require('minio')` or `require('openai')`
- Services: pure functions where possible, explicit error propagation (throw, don't swallow)
- DB: all queries as `db.prepare(...)` statements at module load time, never inside functions

## Express Patterns
```javascript
// Correct async controller pattern
const myHandler = async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const result = await myService.doWork(req.body)
    res.json(result)
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('[myHandler]', err.message)
    res.status(500).json({ error: err.message || 'Internal server error' })
  }
}
```

## HTTP Status Codes
| Situation | Code |
|-----------|------|
| Created resource | 201 |
| Successful GET/PATCH | 200 |
| Bad client input | 400 |
| Not found | 404 |
| File too large | 413 |
| Server error | 500 |

## SQL Rules
- All queries are prepared statements (`db.prepare(...)`) loaded at startup
- Named parameters (`@param`) not positional `?` — clearer for multi-param queries
- WAL mode always enabled (already set in `db/database.js`)
- Never construct SQL strings with user input (even inside services)

## File Upload Rules
- Multer is the only middleware that touches `req.file`
- Validate MIME type in `fileFilter` — allowed: `image/jpeg`, `image/png`, `image/webp`
- Always use `path.basename()` before any file system access on user-supplied filenames
- Temp files must be deleted after MinIO upload (or on failure)

## Environment Config
- All config via `process.env` — never hardcode URLs, ports, or credentials
- Optional services (AI, MinIO): check env var presence, degrade gracefully if absent
- Log mode at startup: `[AI] Mode: GPT-4o vision` or `stub`

## Logging
- Format: `[Service] message` e.g. `[AI]`, `[Storage]`, `[ERROR]`
- Log errors with `console.error('[context]', err.message)`
- Log key state changes at `console.log` level
- Never log request bodies or file contents (could contain PII)
